{
  "id": "agendas",
  "note": "The six intents, what each keeps in store, what each builds, and what moves a governor toward each (governor-agendas.md sections 2, 3, 7, 11, 12, 13). Stocks are per thousand people. A menu is walked top to bottom and the first entry that is wanted (every 'when' holds), reachable, placeable and not already built is taken; nothing taken is 'no building', which is implicit at the end of every menu. Conditions are ids in the code-side registry. The considerations table is the Author's: a row measures how much of a problem one thing is in the town, nought to one, and a cell is how strongly that problem at its worst pushes toward an intent. Education has no cells, since only an urging reaches it. native_aversion is how much an intent minds building on native land, nought to one (section 8, Author ruling 422): a tile deep in it is worth 1 - aversion of the same tile outside. Every threshold is a placeholder.",
